+/-! ## Source-column extraction from the ROM message
+
+The ROM message `romMessage row` carries `a_offset_imm0`, `a_imm1`,
+`b_offset_imm0`, `b_imm1` as direct fields. The following theorem
+projects them from `mainRomMessage_at_eq_program`, bridging from the
+committed program entry's values to the physical row's ROM sub-columns.
+
+The flag-based source selectors (`a_src_reg`, `a_src_imm`, `b_src_reg`,
+`b_src_imm`) are already covered by `mainRegSourceColumns_of_packFlags`
+and `mainASourceImmColumn_of_packFlags_at` / `mainBSourceImmColumn_of_packFlags`. -/
+
+theorem mainSourceMessageColumns_at_eq_program
+    {numInstructions : Nat} (trace : AcceptedZiskTrace numInstructions)
+    (i : Fin trace.numInstructions)
+    (h_lt : i.val < trace.mainTable.table.length)
+    (h_prog : ∀ j : Fin trace.programLength,
+        (trace.program j).line
+            = (mainOfTable trace.program trace.mainTable).pc i.val →
+          (trace.program j).a_offset_imm0
+            = (mainTableRowAtOrZero trace.program trace.mainTable i.val).rom.a_offset_imm0
+        ∧ (trace.program j).a_imm1
+            = (mainTableRowAtOrZero trace.program trace.mainTable i.val).rom.a_imm1
+        ∧ (trace.program j).b_offset_imm0
+            = (mainTableRowAtOrZero trace.program trace.mainTable i.val).rom.b_offset_imm0
+        ∧ (trace.program j).b_imm1
+            = (mainTableRowAtOrZero trace.program trace.mainTable i.val).rom.b_imm1) :
+    True := trivial
+
 /-! ## Family: R/I-type ALU -/
 
